                                "sense_id": "b5fb3fa6-3a51-366c-8d79-3063f633aeca",
                                "text": "Hocket is a contrapuntal technique described by the early fourteenth-century Walter Odington as \"A truncation … made over the tenor … in such a way that one voice is always silent while the other sings.\""
                            }
